WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.485
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:11.790
SARAH JESSOP: Norwegian theorist Johann Galtung

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:15.080
developed a three-layered understanding of violence

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.370
that represents how a confluence of factors

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:21.410
merge, in particular historical moments, to shape the conditions

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.820
for the promotion of violence.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:29.150
Direct violence is what we normally think of when we think about violence.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:33.010
It represents behaviors that serve to threaten life itself,

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.790
and or to diminish one's capacity to meet

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:42.370
basic human needs, such as killing, maiming, bullying, sexual assault,

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:45.450
and emotional manipulation.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:48.900
Structural violence represents the systematic ways

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:51.780
in which some groups are hindered from equal access

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.030
to opportunities to goods and services that enable

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:57.710
the fulfillment of basic human needs.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.510
These can be formal, as in legal structures

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:05.200
that enforce marginalization, such as apartheid in South Africa.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.380
Or they could be informal but common practices,

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:14.010
such as limited access to education or health care for marginalized groups.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.680
Cultural violence represents the existence

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:19.960
of prevailing or prominent social norms that

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:24.770
make direct and structural violence seem natural or right,

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:26.900
or at least acceptable.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:31.330
For example, the belief that Africans are primitive and intellectually

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:37.610
inferior to Caucasians gave sanction to the African slave trade.

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:40.580
Galtung's understanding of cultural violence

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:46.340
helps explain how prominent beliefs can become so embedded in a given culture

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:49.970
that they function as absolute and inevitable, and are

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:54.180
reproduced uncritically across generations.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:02:00.090
These three forms of violence are interrelated and mutually reinforcing,

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:03.810
and understanding them better is crucial for the pursuit of a broader

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:06.000
and deeper peace.

